# The first TLS record on both tracks is an alert, so the parser never
# leaves the started states: state rules are only evaluated when the
# parser's progress moves through a state (the hello record moves it
# out of client_started), so neither rule below can fire here.
#
# client_started (sid 1002) is the rename of the old client_in_progress:
# it is the state the flow IS in, but its decision point only arrives
# when a hello record is seen - which never happens in this session.
# client_hello (sid 1001) is the phase state that is never entered.
#
# The flow is therefore dropped by the implicit default app policy at
# teardown, with every packet accepted in transit.
accept:hook tls:client_started $HOME_NET any -> $HOME_NET any (alert; sid:1002; msg:"client_started state evaluated";)
drop:flow tls:client_hello $HOME_NET any -> $HOME_NET any (alert; sid:1001; msg:"client_hello phase entered on a non-hello first record";)
